WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.735
Twenty-eight landings, twenty-six on this map.

00:03.394 --> 00:11.969
NASA's table of what lies on the Moon, last updated in August 2025, lists 28 landings, six of them with people aboard.

00:12.465 --> 00:19.345
This map marks 26 of them, two by where their rovers stopped, and Chang'e 3's rover Yutu beside its lander.

00:19.949 --> 00:24.811
Luna 9, the first of all, is not one: nobody knows exactly where it is.
